#: ../../source/docs/common-tkoff-rpm-min.rst:5
#: bae10000172d4cb099e0d2a11fa32e6d
msgid "Damaged Motor/Prop Takeoff Prevention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tkoff-rpm-min.rst:7
#: 55bed192d7dd4da0b6b988f8fcfc31af
msgid "Ardupilot provides mechanism to prevent flips on takeoff if a motor, or motors, is not operating at a minimum rpm due to damage. It requires that ESC RPM telemetry is being used. See the ``ESC Telemetry - Average Motor RPM`` section of :ref:`common-rpm` for setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tkoff-rpm-min.rst:9
#: 101a9d8589494d81bef1b91a9497ba4a
msgid "Setting the :ref:`TKOFF_RPM_MIN<TKOFF_RPM_MIN>` slightly below the :ref:`MOT_SPIN_ARM <MOT_SPIN_ARM>`, if the average rpm is lower than this, throttle increases will not be passed on, preventing a takeoff and an immediate flip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-tkoff-rpm-min.rst:11
#: 5830e86ee0204ef2a46f3b881bf63da9
msgid "The :ref:`TKOFF_RPM_MAX <TKOFF_RPM_MAX>` parameter can also be used to assure that a propeller is not missing or loose."
msgstr ""
